  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Car dealer Don Wheaton persuaded General Motors to let him expand beyond its usual limit of one dealership per owner. When a Calgary franchise became available, his relationship with the manufacturer's leadership helped him secure an exception. Buying that second dealership allowed him to extend his business beyond Edmonton.\n\nHe and his family later developed financial products for customers buying cars through dealerships. They began with creditor life and disability insurance, then added extended warranties. General Bank of Canada followed, issuing its first car loan in 2005 with a staff of three.",
